%% Sequence 1: bring-up in the ideal scenario. Built: skeleton.launch.py, lifecycle_manager_core. Planned: lifecycle_sequencer, manager_nav, manager_optional (PR #12, 005-R35).
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant L as skeleton.launch.py (built)
  participant IA as IA368II manager and nodes (built, own config)
  participant PL as twist_mux, wheel bridge, teleop (plain, third-party)
  participant SQ as lifecycle_sequencer (PLANNED, plain, D-26)
  participant CO as lifecycle_manager_core (built)
  participant NV as lifecycle_manager_nav (PLANNED)
  participant OP as lifecycle_manager_optional (PLANNED, empty)

  L->>PL: start twist_mux with twist_mux.yaml (use_stamped false)
  L->>IA: start myrobot, behaviour_server, cleaning and autodocking servers
  Note over IA: IA368II manager configures and activates its own nodes
  IA-->>L: nodes active, mode CHARGED on /myRobot/behaviour/mode
  L->>SQ: start sequencer (planned)
  Note over L,CO: today the launch starts lifecycle_manager_core directly (autostart)
  SQ->>CO: bring up core
  CO->>CO: configure and activate stop_guard first
  Note over CO: the safety net exists before anything can move
  CO->>CO: activate stuck_detector, escape_server, coverage_server
  CO->>CO: activate supervisor last
  Note over CO: supervisor sends goals as soon as it is active
  CO-->>SQ: is_active true (or failed after manager_startup_timeout_s 30 s)
  alt core failed
    SQ-->>SQ: FAILED_CORE, nav and optional not started, ERROR CORE_START_FAILED on /myRobot/notifications
  else core active
    SQ->>NV: start nav (planner_server, controller_server, bt_navigator)
    NV-->>SQ: is_active true (nav failure means degraded, no automatic motion)
    SQ->>OP: start optional (cloud, MQTT, spec 009b)
    OP-->>SQ: is_active true (failure is ignored, Art. VII)
  end
